The balanced-hyperedge sweep did expose a hard low-degree window, but it has no compact route after the insight; it would violate G9 by testing blind CSP search. I’m therefore using the paper’s Reduction Lemma instead: every Venn region is built from XOR-paired elements, and the submitted witness is an exact symbolic splitter (a common translation plus an affine parity selector). This gives an honest Track B gap between full stabilizer search and a short two-set symmetry intersection.
