Implemented the verified Track B generator, but it is not yet shippable because OpenRouter quota blocked every oracle call.

- [gen_1611_01542.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1611.01542/gen_1611_01542.py) — deterministic inverse-generated native p-splittability instances.
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1611.01542/selftest_report.json) — all nine locally gated checks pass.
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1611.01542/README.md) — construction, paper grounding, example, measurements, and caveats.
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1611.01542/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl) — bare-run HTTP 403 evidence.
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1611.01542/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl) and [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1611.01542/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl) — likewise blocked by quota.

Key measurements:

- Track B, native combinatorics/exact cover.
- Random guesses: 0/200,000.
- Four adversarial attacks: each 0/8.
- Algorithm X: 8/8, averaging 88,394 nodes.
- Answer: at most 323 characters, 81 estimated tokens, 40 elements.
- Compact route: 216 operations.
- Canonical-key checks: 60/60 invariant; 20/20 unrelated instances distinct.

The repository validator confirms all gates pass and blocks only on the missing scored hardening transcript. No `REJECTED.md` was written because this is an external quota failure, not a failure of G, H, or V.
