The paper check supports the exact-cover formulation: for `p=1/d` and `d`-element rows, a splitter is exactly a set of incidence columns covering every row once. It also confirms that the NP-completeness theorem is only worst-case, while the draft’s efficient solvers make Track A untenable; Track B is the only honest route. I’m now stress-testing whether the planted modular progression is actually a compact, discoverable structure and whether the self-test’s measurements are sound.
